# =============================================================================
# NEXUS — frontend environment template (apps/web)
#
# Copy to apps/web/.env.local for local work, or set these in Vercel for
# Production and Preview separately (DEPLOYMENT.md §4).
#
# Only `PUBLIC_`-prefixed values reach the browser — SvelteKit enforces this, and
# it is the mechanism behind the project's first security rule. Never put
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, an AI API key, or DATABASE_URL in this file:
# src/lib/utils/env.ts only reads PUBLIC_* names, so such a value would either be
# ignored or, worse, be readable by anyone with the bundle.
# =============================================================================

# --- Supabase (public by design) ---------------------------------------------
# Safe in the browser: every table they can reach is guarded by RLS.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- API base URL ------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave EMPTY to call the API on this app's own origin at `/api/v1/...`, which
# `vite.config.ts` proxies to FastAPI in development. That is the default
# because it is the one configuration that is correct both locally and in
# production — a deployed browser can never reach `127.0.0.1`.
#
# Set it only when the API is on a different origin, and then also add this
# app's origin to the API's CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS:
#   PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://nexus-api.fly.dev
PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# The spec's name for the same setting. NOT readable by the browser (missing the
# PUBLIC_ prefix, by design), but the dev proxy reads it in Node — so setting
# only this still points local development at the right backend.
# API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1
